   and tables, and the parts of utils.h and utils.cpp those use (src/bc7decomp.rs,
   src/bc7enc.rs, src/rgbcx.rs, src/rgbcx_tables.rs, src/ert.rs, src/rdo_bc_encoder.rs,
   src/image.rs).

    Copyright(c) 2020-2021 Richard Geldreich, Jr.

   Those files are offered by their author under the MIT licence or as public domain
   (unlicense.org), whichever the user prefers; that notice is kept in LICENSE-bc7enc_rdo.txt.

   They are changed here in that they are translated from C++ to Rust: the tables the C++
   keeps in globals are values, and the entry points have Rust's names. What they compute is
   kept: they give the same blocks as the C++ library.

3. bcdec, by Sergii Kudlai (https://github.com/iOrange/bcdec): the BC6H unpacker of its
   bcdec.h (in src/bc6h.rs).

    Copyright (c) 2022 Sergii Kudlai

   That file is offered by its author under the MIT licence or as public domain
